@host = http://localhost:5000

### Mode A (the .NET 11 pipeline) - FAILS: nested, collection and dictionary errors in one ProblemDetails
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "shippingAddress": { "street": "1 Main Street", "city": "", "postCode": "LS1 1AA" },
  "lines": [{ "sku": "abc", "quantity": 0 }],
  "additionalAddresses": { "billing": { "street": "2 High Street", "city": "Leeds", "postCode": "1" } }
}

### Mode A - FAILS, with the messages in French (codes and paths do not change)
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: fr

{
  "customerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "shippingAddress": { "street": "1 Main Street", "city": "", "postCode": "LS1 1AA" },
  "lines": [{ "sku": "abc", "quantity": 0 }]
}

### Mode A - PASSES (201 Created)
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "ann@example.com",
  "shippingAddress": { "street": "1 Main Street", "city": "Leeds", "postCode": "LS1 1AA" },
  "lines": [{ "sku": "ABC-1234", "quantity": 2 }],
  "additionalAddresses": { "billing": { "street": "2 High Street", "city": "Leeds", "postCode": "LS2 2BB" } }
}

### Mode B (WithZodSharpValidation filter) - FAILS with the same contract
POST {{host}}/filtered/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "shippingAddress": { "street": "1 Main Street", "city": "", "postCode": "LS1 1AA" },
  "lines": []
}

### Manual validation (ZodTypedResults.ValidationProblem) - FAILS with the same contract
POST {{host}}/manual/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "ABC-1234", "quantity": 101 }]
}

### Manual validation - PASSES (201 Created)
POST {{host}}/manual/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "ann@example.com",
  "shippingAddress": { "street": "1 Main Street", "city": "Leeds", "postCode": "LS1 1AA" },
  "lines": [{ "sku": "ABC-1234", "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Service-aware async rule - FAILS: taken@example.com is already in the in-memory registry (email_taken)
POST {{host}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ann",
  "email": "taken@example.com",
  "age": 30
}

### Service-aware async rule - PASSES once (201 Created); sending it again FAILS, because it is now registered
POST {{host}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ann",
  "email": "ann@example.com",
  "age": 30
}

### The OpenAPI document: ZodSharp constraints, and ZodValidationProblemDetails on every validated operation
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
